    will be ``2`` and dimension along other axes will be same as that of input.

    >>> with jnp.printoptions(precision=2, suppress=True):
    ...   print(jax.numpy.fft.fftn(x, s=[2], axes=[0]))
    [[ 5.+0.j  3.+0.j  8.+0.j 13.+0.j]
